---
title: "Content Collections Setup and Patterns"
description: "Define and manage Astro content collections with TypeScript schemas, Zod validation, and type-safe querying"
category: "rules"
priority: "high"
alwaysApply: false
tokenEstimate: 350
loadingLevel: 2
tags: ["astro", "content", "collections", "typescript", "validation"]
relatedFiles:
  - "rules/astro/content/frontmatter.mdx"
  - "rules/astro/content/images.mdx"
  - "snippets/astro/frontmatter-schemas.md"
lastUpdated: "2025-11-19"
version: "1.0"
deprecates: null
useWhen:
  - "Setting up new content collections"
  - "Defining collection schemas with Zod"
  - "Querying content and filtering collections"
  - "Working with type-safe content entries"
---

# Content Collections Setup and Patterns

## Collection Structure

Collections in this project are organized in `src/content/`:

```
src/content/
├── blog/              # Blog post entries
├── pages/             # Static page content
└── footer/            # Footer collection entries
```

## Defining Collections with Zod

Collections require a `config.*` file (e.g., `src/content/config.ts`) with TypeScript interfaces and Zod schemas:

### Pattern: Collection Configuration

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Type-safe collection with Zod schema
import { defineCollection, z } from 'astro:content';

const blogCollection = defineCollection({
  type: 'content',
  schema: z.object({
    title: z.string(),
    description: z.string(),
    pubDate: z.coerce.date(),
    updatedDate: z.coerce.date().optional(),
    heroImage: z.string().optional(),
    tags: z.array(z.string()).default([]),
    author: z.string().optional(),
  }),
});

export const collections = {
  blog: blogCollection,
  pages: defineCollection({
    type: 'content',
    schema: z.object({
      title: z.string(),
      description: z.string(),
    }),
  }),
};
```

### Anti-pattern: Unvalidated Collections

```typescript
// ❌ Bad: Missing schema validation
const collections = {
  blog: defineCollection({ type: 'content' }),
};
```

## Querying Collections

### Pattern: Type-Safe Collection Queries

```typescript
import { getCollection, type CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';

// ✅ Get all entries
const allPosts = await getCollection('blog');

// ✅ Filter with type safety
const publishedPosts = (await getCollection('blog')).filter(
  (post) => !post.data.draft
);

// ✅ Sort by date
const sortedPosts = allPosts.sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf()
);

// ✅ Get specific entry by slug
const post = await getCollection('blog').then(
  (posts) => posts.find((p) => p.slug === 'my-post')
);
```

### Anti-pattern: Untyped Collection Access

```typescript
// ❌ Bad: No type safety or filtering
const posts: any = await getCollection('blog');
const firstPost = posts[0];
```

## Collection Entry Types

### Pattern: Using CollectionEntry Type

```typescript
import type { CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';

type BlogPost = CollectionEntry<'blog'>;

interface BlogPostWithId extends BlogPost {
  id: string;
}

// ✅ Type-safe function signature
async function getBlogPostById(
  id: string
): Promise<BlogPost | undefined> {
  return (await getCollection('blog')).find((post) => post.id === id);
}

// ✅ In components/pages
export interface Props {
  post: CollectionEntry<'blog'>;
}

const { post } = Astro.props;
```

## Dynamic Route Generation

### Pattern: Generate Routes from Collections

```typescript
// src/pages/blog/[...slug].astro
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const blogEntries = await getCollection('blog');
  return blogEntries.map((entry) => ({
    params: { slug: entry.slug },
    props: { entry },
  }));
}

interface Props {
  entry: CollectionEntry<'blog'>;
}

const { entry } = Astro.props;
const { Content } = await entry.render();
```

## Collection Validation

### Pattern: Validate During Build

```typescript
// TypeScript strict mode catches schema violations at build time
// Zod provides runtime validation for dynamic content

// ✅ Schema violation caught at build time
// If you add a post without required fields, `pnpm typecheck` fails

// ✅ Custom validation
const schema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(3, 'Title must be at least 3 characters'),
  tags: z.array(z.string()).min(1, 'At least one tag required'),
});
```

## Related Content Patterns

### Pattern: Query Related Entries

```typescript
// ✅ Find posts by tag
async function getPostsByTag(tag: string) {
  const allPosts = await getCollection('blog');
  return allPosts.filter((post) => post.data.tags.includes(tag));
}

// ✅ Get n latest posts
async function getLatestPosts(limit: number = 5) {
  const posts = await getCollection('blog');
  return posts
    .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf())
    .slice(0, limit);
}
```

## Key Principles

- Always use Zod schemas for collection validation
- Define explicit TypeScript interfaces alongside schemas
- Use `CollectionEntry<'collection-name'>` for type-safe entry handling
- Filter and sort at query time, not at render time
- Validate required fields with Zod (no optional fields unless needed)
- Use content collection routes for dynamic page generation

