# Build Performance Optimization

## Static Generation Best Practices

### Pattern: Optimize Static Generation

```astro
---
// ✅ Good: Leverage Astro's static generation
// This page is pre-rendered at build time
// No server needed for deployment

interface Props {
  title: string;
  content: string;
}

const { title, content } = Astro.props;

// Pre-computed data from collections
// No dynamic requests at runtime
---

<article>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <div>{content}</div>
</article>
```

### Anti-pattern: Dynamic Rendering

```astro
---
// ❌ Bad: Dynamic data fetching delays page load
const response = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data');
const data = await response.json();

// This happens during page rendering, not at build time
---

<div>{data.content}</div>
```

## Code Splitting Strategy

### Pattern: Conditional Island Hydration

```astro
---
import ThemeToggle from '../components/ui/ThemeToggle.astro';
import InteractiveComponent from '../components/interactive/InteractiveComponent.astro';

// ✅ Good: Only hydrate components that need interactivity
---

<header>
  {/* Static content - no JavaScript */}
  <h1>Site Title</h1>

  {/* Interactive component - hydrated on demand */}
  <ThemeToggle client:idle />
</header>

<main>
  {/* Static blog content */}
  <slot />

  {/* Interactive features - loaded when visible */}
  <InteractiveComponent client:visible />
</main>
```

### Client Directive Guide

```astro
---
// Hydration strategies for component interactivity

// ✅ load immediately - Use for critical interactions
<Button client:load />

// ✅ load after page render - Use for important features
<Sidebar client:idle />

// ✅ load when in viewport - Use for non-critical below-fold content
<Gallery client:visible />

// ✅ load on component interaction - Use for optional features
<Modal client:only />

// ✅ Never hydrate - Use for static content
<Card />
---
```

## Bundle Size Optimization

### Pattern: Dynamic Imports for Large Components

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Load heavy component only when needed
import { lazy } from 'preact';

export const HeavyChart = lazy(
  () => import('../components/charts/HeavyChart')
);
```

### Pattern: Analyze Bundle Size

```bash
# ✅ Analyze what's in your bundle
npm run build --analyze

# Check individual page sizes
ls -lh dist/

# Output: Identifies large files and optimization opportunities
```

### Component Weight Considerations

| Component Type | Bundle Impact | Hydration Strategy |
|---|---|---|
| **Button/Badge** | < 1KB | Never (static) |
| **Form/Input** | 5-10KB | client:idle |
| **Modal/Dialog** | 10-15KB | client:only |
| **Chart/Graph** | 50-100KB | client:visible |
| **3D/Game** | 100KB+ | client:only |

## Build Optimization Configuration

### Pattern: astro.config.mts Optimization

```typescript
// astro.config.mts
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';
import tailwind from '@astrojs/tailwind';

export default defineConfig({
  // ✅ Good: Enable static generation
  output: 'static',

  // ✅ Good: Enable compression
  compressHTML: true,

  // ✅ Good: Minify CSS and JS
  vite: {
    build: {
      minify: 'terser',
      terserOptions: {
        compress: {
          drop_console: true,
        },
      },
    },
  },

  // ✅ Good: Optimize images
  image: {
    service: {
      entrypoint: 'astro/assets/services/sharp',
    },
  },

  integrations: [
    tailwind({
      // ✅ Good: Use CSS optimization
      applyBaseStyles: false,
    }),
  ],
});
```

## Caching Strategies

### Pattern: Static Asset Caching

```typescript
// Astro automatically handles versioning for optimal caching
// Built files include content hash: bundle.abc123.js

// For production deployments:
// 1. CSS/JS files: Cache forever (content-hash in filename)
// 2. HTML files: Cache-Control: max-age=3600 (1 hour)
// 3. Images: Cache-Control: max-age=86400 (1 day)
```

### Pattern: Service Worker for Offline Support

```typescript
// ✅ Optional: Implement service worker for offline support
// Install @astrojs/service-worker if needed

// src/service-worker.ts
/// <reference lib="webworker" />

declare const self: ServiceWorkerGlobalScope;

const cacheName = 'astro-cache-v1';

self.addEventListener('install', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil(self.skipWaiting());
});

self.addEventListener('activate', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil(self.clients.claim());
});

self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  if (event.request.method !== 'GET') return;

  event.respondWith(
    caches.match(event.request)
      .then((response) => response || fetch(event.request))
      .then((response) => {
        if (!response) return response;
        const responseToCache = response.clone();
        caches.open(cacheName).then((cache) => {
          cache.put(event.request, responseToCache);
        });
        return response;
      })
      .catch(() => new Response('Offline'))
  );
});
```

## Image Optimization at Build Time

### Pattern: Image Optimization

```astro
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import heroImage from '../images/hero.png';

// ✅ Good: Astro optimizes at build time
// - Converts to WebP/AVIF
// - Generates responsive sizes
// - Creates srcset automatically
---

<Image
  src={heroImage}
  alt="Hero"
  width={1200}
  height={675}
  class="w-full h-auto"
/>
```

## Font Loading Optimization

### Pattern: Font Strategies

```astro
---
// ✅ Good: Preload critical fonts
// ✅ Good: Use system fonts as fallback
---

<!-- Preload only critical font weights -->
<link
  rel="preload"
  href="/fonts/inter-400.woff2"
  as="font"
  type="font/woff2"
  crossorigin
/>

<!-- Font-display: swap for better LCP -->
<style>
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Inter';
    src: url('/fonts/inter-400.woff2') format('woff2');
    font-display: swap;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  body {
    /* ✅ Good: System fonts fallback */
    font-family: Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto;
  }
</style>
```

## CSS Optimization

### Pattern: Tailwind CSS Optimization

```css
/* ✅ Good: Tailwind automatically purges unused styles */
/* Only included classes used in HTML/components are in production bundle */

@import "tailwindcss";

/* ✅ Good: Use CSS custom properties for dynamic values */
:root {
  --color-primary: oklch(0.65 0.12 260);
}

body {
  color: var(--color-primary);
}
```

## Build Performance Monitoring

### Performance Targets

| Metric | Target | Impact |
|--------|--------|--------|
| **Build Time** | < 60s | Development experience |
| **HTML Size** | < 50KB | Network transfer |
| **JS Bundle** | < 100KB | Core Web Vitals |
| **CSS Bundle** | < 20KB | Paint timing |
| **Total HTML** | < 200KB | Mobile speed |

## Build Optimization Checklist

- [ ] Output is static (not on-demand SSR)
- [ ] HTML compression enabled
- [ ] CSS/JS minification active
- [ ] Image optimization configured
- [ ] Unused CSS purged via Tailwind
- [ ] Service worker optional (if offline needed)
- [ ] Critical fonts preloaded
- [ ] Font-display: swap used
- [ ] Code splitting with dynamic imports
- [ ] No synchronous scripts in head
- [ ] Preload critical resources
- [ ] DNS prefetch for external domains
- [ ] Gzip/Brotli compression enabled on server
- [ ] Cache headers configured
- [ ] CDN in use for static assets

## Performance Debugging

```bash
# ✅ Analyze bundle size
npm run build

# Check individual page sizes
du -sh dist/

# Inspect what's in the build
ls -lh dist/**/*.js

# Test locally before deploy
npm run preview
