# Image Optimization in Astro

## Using Astro Image Component

### Pattern: Basic Image Usage

```astro
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import heroImg from '../images/hero.png';
---

<!-- ✅ Good: Using Image component with static import -->
<Image
  src={heroImg}
  alt="Hero image for landing page"
  width={1200}
  height={675}
  class="w-full h-auto"
/>
```

### Anti-pattern: Raw img Tag

```astro
<!-- ❌ Bad: No optimization, no responsive sizing -->
<img src="/images/hero.png" alt="Hero image" />

<!-- ❌ Bad: Manual optimization without Astro Image -->
<img src="/images/hero.webp" alt="Hero" width="1200" height="675" />
```

## Responsive Images

### Pattern: Responsive Image Sizing

```astro
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import contentImg from '../images/blog-feature.webp';
---

<!-- ✅ Good: Responsive with aspect ratio preservation -->
<div class="aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
  <Image
    src={contentImg}
    alt="Blog feature image"
    width={1200}
    height={675}
    class="w-full h-full object-cover"
  />
</div>
```

### Pattern: Hero Image with Responsive Aspect Ratio

```astro
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

interface Props {
  src: ImageMetadata;
  alt: string;
  title: string;
}

const { src, alt, title } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="w-full bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-900">
  <div class="aspect-[2/1] md:aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
    <Image
      src={src}
      alt={alt}
      width={1200}
      height={675}
      class="w-full h-full object-cover"
    />
  </div>
  <h1 class="mt-4">{title}</h1>
</section>
```

## Image Formats and Optimization

### Pattern: Format Selection

```astro
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
---

<!-- ✅ Good: Let Astro handle format optimization -->
<!-- Astro automatically serves AVIF/WebP where supported, PNG fallback -->
<Image
  src={imageImport}
  alt="Optimized image"
  width={800}
  height={600}
/>
```

### Image Format Guidelines

| Format | Best For | Browser Support |
|--------|----------|-----------------|
| **AVIF** | Photo quality, maximum compression | Modern browsers |
| **WebP** | Good quality-to-size ratio | All modern browsers |
| **PNG** | Transparency, lossless | All browsers (fallback) |
| **JPG** | Legacy support, photos | All browsers |

## Dynamic Image Sources

### Pattern: Image from Content Collections

```astro
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import type { CollectionEntry } from 'astro:content';

interface Props {
  post: CollectionEntry<'blog'>;
}

const { post } = Astro.props;
---

{post.data.heroImage && (
  <div class="aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
    <Image
      src={post.data.heroImage}
      alt={`Hero image for ${post.data.title}`}
      width={1200}
      height={675}
      class="w-full h-full object-cover"
    />
  </div>
)}
```

### Anti-pattern: Remote URLs

```astro
<!-- ❌ Bad: No optimization for remote images -->
<img src="https://example.com/image.jpg" alt="Remote image" />

<!-- ✅ Better: Use Image component with remote URL support -->
<Image
  src="https://example.com/image.jpg"
  alt="Remote image"
  width={1200}
  height={675}
/>
```

## Image Gallery Pattern

### Pattern: Responsive Image Grid

```astro
---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import image1 from '../images/gallery-1.webp';
import image2 from '../images/gallery-2.webp';
import image3 from '../images/gallery-3.webp';

const images = [image1, image2, image3];
---

<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  {images.map((img) => (
    <div class="aspect-square overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
      <Image
        src={img}
        alt="Gallery image"
        width={400}
        height={400}
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  ))}
</div>
```

## Performance Considerations

### Lazy Loading

```astro
<!-- ✅ Good: Lazy loading for below-fold images -->
<Image
  src={belowFoldImage}
  alt="Below-fold content"
  loading="lazy"
  decoding="async"
  width={800}
  height={600}
/>

<!-- ✅ Good: Eager loading for above-fold images -->
<Image
  src={heroImage}
  alt="Hero image"
  loading="eager"
  decoding="sync"
  width={1200}
  height={675}
/>
```

### Image Sizing Best Practices

```astro
---
// ✅ Good: Use natural aspect ratios
// Hero: 16:9 (1200x675)
// Card: 3:4 (300x400)
// Square: 1:1 (400x400)
// Thumbnail: 2:1 (200x100)
---

<Image
  src={image}
  alt="Correctly proportioned image"
  width={1200}
  height={675}
/>
```

## Type-Safe Image Imports

### Pattern: ImageMetadata Type

```astro
---
import { Image, type ImageMetadata } from 'astro:assets';
import heroImg from '../images/hero.webp';

interface Props {
  image: ImageMetadata;
  alt: string;
}

const { image, alt } = Astro.props;
---

<Image
  src={image}
  alt={alt}
  class="w-full h-auto"
/>
```

## Image Optimization Checklist

- Use Astro's Image component for all content images
- Provide explicit width and height (aspect ratio preservation)
- Use semantic alt text for accessibility
- Set loading="lazy" for below-fold images
- Set loading="eager" for hero/above-fold images
- Keep images under 500KB (Astro optimizes automatically)
- Use static imports when possible
- Serve WebP/AVIF with PNG/JPG fallbacks
- Test Core Web Vitals (LCP < 2.5s)
- Validate responsive sizing on mobile/tablet/desktop

