# Build Performance Optimization

## Static Generation Best Practices

### Pattern: Optimize Static Generation

```astro
---
// ✅ Good: Leverage Astro's static generation
// This page is pre-rendered at build time
// No server needed for deployment

interface Props {
  title: string;
  content: string;
}

const { title, content } = Astro.props;

// Pre-computed data from collections
// No dynamic requests at runtime
---

<article>
  <h1>{title}</h1>
  <div>{content}</div>
</article>
```

### Anti-pattern: Dynamic Rendering

```astro
---
// ❌ Bad: Dynamic data fetching delays page load
const response = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data');
const data = await response.json();

// This happens during page rendering, not at build time
---

<div>{data.content}</div>
```

## Code Splitting Strategy

### Pattern: Conditional Island Hydration

```astro
---
import ThemeToggle from '../components/ui/ThemeToggle.astro';
import InteractiveComponent from '../components/interactive/InteractiveComponent.astro';

// ✅ Good: Only hydrate components that need interactivity
---

<header>
  {/* Static content - no JavaScript */}
  <h1>Site Title</h1>

  {/* Interactive component - hydrated on demand */}
  <ThemeToggle client:idle />
</header>

<main>
  {/* Static blog content */}
  <slot />

  {/* Interactive features - loaded when visible */}
  <InteractiveComponent client:visible />
</main>
```

### Client Directive Guide

```astro
---
// Hydration strategies for component interactivity

// ✅ load immediately - Use for critical interactions
<Button client:load />

// ✅ load after page render - Use for important features
<Sidebar client:idle />

// ✅ load when in viewport - Use for non-critical below-fold content
<Gallery client:visible />

// ✅ load on component interaction - Use for optional features
<Modal client:only />

// ✅ Never hydrate - Use for static content
<Card />
---
```

## Bundle Size Optimization

### Pattern: Dynamic Imports for Large Components

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Load heavy component only when needed
import { lazy } from 'preact';

export const HeavyChart = lazy(
  () => import('../components/charts/HeavyChart')
);
```

### Pattern: Analyze Bundle Size

```bash
# ✅ Analyze what's in your bundle
npm run build --analyze

# Check individual page sizes
ls -lh dist/

# Output: Identifies large files and optimization opportunities
```

### Component Weight Considerations

| Component Type | Bundle Impact | Hydration Strategy |
|---|---|---|
| **Button/Badge** | < 1KB | Never (static) |
| **Form/Input** | 5-10KB | client:idle |
| **Modal/Dialog** | 10-15KB | client:only |
| **Chart/Graph** | 50-100KB | client:visible |
| **3D/Game** | 100KB+ | client:only |

